            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="FAL02" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Captain</roleName>
                        <forename>Charles John</forename>
                        <surname>Carey</surname>
                        <addName>Cary</addName>
                        <addName>ninth Viscount Falkland</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1768">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1809"/>
                    <occupation>captain in the Navy</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial"><p>See <persName key="FAL01">Henry Thomas Carey Falkland</persName></p>.
    
    <p>Charles Carey was Henry Carey's successor to the title in 1796, when references in the diary switch from Carey to Falkland. Chales Carey died after a drunken duel with his friend Arthur A. Powell</p><p>Note that there are four unidentified entries for 'Carey' after 1809. viz 
    18.12.1822,  2.09.1823, 3.11.1832, 4.03.1834.  It is possible that these refer to one of Falkland's three sons.</p></note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>, Cary, Lucius Bentinck</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
